## 3. Currency and decimal contract matrix

| Rail | Dart type on the wire | Precision | Currency sent |
|---|---|---|---|
| Friend send/request | `double` (`sendFunds(String, double)`, `friend_service.dart:238-240`; body `'amount': amount` :254) | binary float | USDC |
| Crypto + fiat withdrawal | `double` (`_submitMobileMoney(double)`:429, `_submitCryptoWallet(double)`:598; body :474/:633) | binary float; fees computed client-side as doubles and rendered as USDC (:2078-2096) | USDC |
| Susu contribution | **string** `toStringAsFixed(2)` (`susu_service.dart:110`) | 2 dp, exact text | USDC |
| Vendor internal transfer (main) | `double` | binary float | USDC |
| Vendor internal transfer (**branch** `wip/vendor-transfer-decimal-string`, unmerged) | **string** from a BigInt 8-dp parser | 8 dp exact | USDC |
| Retail checkout | server-priced; client sends items/qty (`storefront_service.dart:686`) | server Decimal | server-side |
| GHS anywhere in money movement | **not present** | — | — |

**Answer to "are GHS amounts silently converted into USDC?": No, verified.** No money-moving path reads a GHS figure. GHS exists only as (a) display valuation (`balance_card_valuation.dart`, `balance_card_valuation_provider.dart`), (b) oracle/rate alerts, (c) quote/liability surfaces. The valuation provider is consumed by exactly two display widgets (`large_text_deck_sheet.dart:71`, balance-card widgets) and by **no** money path.

**Answer to "does the app treat a display valuation as spendable?": No, verified** by exhaustive reference search: `balanceCardValuationProvider` has no consumer outside display widgets; spending reads `availableBalance` from `/auth/me/{id}` (`vendor_dashboard.dart:96`, `withdrawal_screen.dart:367`) and `/wallet/history`.

**But the precision class is systemic:** outside susu (2 dp text) and the unmerged vendor branch, every money amount is a Dart `double` serialised into JSON as a number, so 0.1 + 0.2 style drift and >15-significant-digit truncation are possible before the request leaves the device. The exact-string parser and bound work done for `/wallet/internal-transfer` has **not** been applied to friend transfers or withdrawals.

---

## 4. Authentication and idempotency matrix

| Control | Where | Verified behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| Bearer auth | `ApiClient` interceptor + refresh (`_tryRefreshToken`, `api_client.dart:613`) | 401 auto-refresh then rethrow |
| PIN gate | `showCardPinGate` (`home_screen.dart:1113`) | used for card surface |
| Biometric pre-gate | `utils/biometric_gate.dart`, used `transfer_modal.dart:428`, `invoice_detail_screen.dart:24` | pre-flight, cancellable |
| Biometric lock setting | `security_settings.dart:73` via `BiometricService` | toggle |
| Step-up header | — | **no `X-2FA`/step-up header found anywhere in `lib/`** while backend mounts `require2FA()` on financial routes (e.g. `walletRoutes.js` internal-transfer). How this client satisfies that gate is **unverified**. |
| Header idempotency | `postFinancial` (`api_client.dart:196`) + `DurableOperationRegistry` | key armed before first send; same key on retry; **retire on 2xx / definitive 4xx**, retain on 401/409/429/5xx/network |
| Body idempotency | storefront + escrow + EWA + savings | key in body, same lifecycle semantics |
| No idempotency | invoice pay, auction bid, azm-stake, group-chat susu, susu invites/auto-retain, deposit OTP | a lost response on these is **not** recoverable with the same identity |

**Duplicate-execution answer:** for `postFinancial` rails, a retry inside one live session reuses the key (safe). After a process restart the `FinancialOperationRef` is a fresh empty holder (`api_client.dart:737-743`, created per State), so a lost-response request re-submitted after restart gets a **new** key and can duplicate. This is pre-existing and rail-wide, not specific to any one screen. Recovery is possible only through the explicit recovery surface (`postFinancialRecovered`), which replays an immutable stored snapshot under the original key.

