**All three support single-transaction token consumption without restructuring.** The conditional-update idiom already exists — `commitOperation`'s CAS is the same shape a token consumption needs.

## 3. Binding completeness

Server-authoritative, must be bound: user id; action + subtype (`/withdraw` vs `/withdraw/fiat` vs `/internal-transfer` distinct endpoints); destination identity; asset/currency; exact debit (`toExactDecimal` result, not the raw body); **effective fee inputs** — `GlobalSettings.withdrawalFeeByRiskTier`, `fiatWithdrawalFeePct`/`baseExitFeePct`, discount multiplier (`finance.service.js:108-125`) plus a settings version/hash, because these are mutable rows; total debit; idempotency key (`userId,endpoint,key`); route identity.

